      bearCase: "Intensifying geopolitical tensions, particularly between the US and China, could lead to tech decoupling, disrupting global supply chains and limiting market access. High-stakes IP litigation in AI (Apple vs. OpenAI) may stifle collaboration and innovation, while increased regulatory scrutiny on both AI and crypto could impose significant compliance burdens, hindering growth and profitability.",
      neutralCase: "The market will likely see continued innovation in AI and robotics, balanced by ongoing competition and regulatory challenges. While Unitree\'s IPO is a strong signal, global tech markets will remain volatile. Crypto\'s political influence will grow, but its impact on policy will be incremental rather than revolutionary, leading to a complex but manageable environment for tech-focused investors.",
      probabilityWeightedOutlook: "We assign a 50% probability to a \'neutral\' scenario of continued growth tempered by competition and regulation, a 30% probability to a \'bullish\' scenario driven by rapid innovation and favorable policy shifts, and a 20% probability to a \'bearish\' scenario characterized by escalating tech wars and stifling regulation. The most likely path involves navigating a dynamic landscape with both significant opportunities and notable risks.",
